{
  "$comment": "Subscription-plan variants for bin/fm-strategy.sh --plans. why holds the rule text a plan render opens each requested-worker and tier why with; the rendered routes complete it. Each mode lists a role as \"<model> <effort>\"; the light, standard, and hard tiers may instead list an ordered ladder of routes from stronger to cheaper, each \"<model> <effort> <floor>\" except the last, where <floor> is the all_models percent below which the resolver steps down to the next route. The last light and standard route takes the plan's floors value, below which the tier leaves the provider, and the last hard route is never floored. A plan with same_as takes its profile from that plan and keeps its own label and full_warning; a plan without floors writes none on its last routes. docs/configuration.md \"Token strategies\" owns the contract.",
  "why": {
    "requested": "Honor the requested worker. A requested worker skips tier routing, so it gets this plan's pin:",
    "light": "Tier 1. Mechanical work; the cheapest capable model.",
    "standard": "Tier 2. Most everyday work.",
    "hard": "Tier 3. Keep the provider's strongest model where mistakes are expensive; a step down only lowers its effort and the last route is never floored, so hard work never drops to a weaker model.",
    "ladder": "Within one provider the first route whose floor still holds is used, so a falling quota steps down to the cheaper route before the week runs out."
  },
